Supreme People's Court

Issuance of the Notice on the Provisions on the Division of Trial Work for Intellectual Property Administrative Cases Concerning Authorization and Confirmation of Patents, Trademarks, Etc.

Fa Fa [2009] No. 39

To the High People's Courts of all provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government; the Military Court of the People's Liberation Army; and the Production and Construction Corps Branch of the High People's Court of Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region:

The Provisions on the Division of Trial Work for Intellectual Property Administrative Cases Concerning Authorization and Confirmation of Patents, Trademarks, Etc. of the Supreme People's Court are hereby issued to you for earnest implementation.

June 26, 2009

Provisions on the Division of Trial Work for Intellectual Property Administrative Cases Concerning Authorization and Confirmation of Patents, Trademarks, Etc.

(Adopted at the 1469th Session of the Judicial Committee of the Supreme People's Court on June 22, 2009)

For the purpose of implementing the Outline of the National Intellectual Property Strategy, improving the intellectual property trial system, and ensuring the uniformity of judicial standards, the division of trial work for intellectual property administrative cases concerning authorization and confirmation of patents, trademarks, etc. is hereby provided as follows:

Article 1 The following cases of first and second instance shall be tried by the relevant intermediate people's courts in Beijing, the Beijing High People's Court, and the Intellectual Property Division of the Supreme People's Court:

(1) Cases不服 (challenging) the patent reexamination decisions and invalidation decisions made by the Patent Reexamination Board of the patent administrative department under the State Council;

(2) Cases不服 (challenging) the decisions on compulsory licensing of patents and the rulings on fees for compulsory licensing of patents made by the patent administrative department under the State Council;

(3) Cases不服 (challenging) the trademark reexamination decisions and rulings made by the Trademark Review and Adjudication Board of the administrative department for industry and commerce under the State Council;

(4) Cases不服 (challenging) the reexamination decisions and revocation decisions on layout designs of integrated circuits made by the intellectual property administrative department under the State Council;

(5) Cases不服 (challenging) the decisions on non-voluntary licensing for the use of layout designs of integrated circuits and the rulings on compensation for non-voluntary licensing for the use of layout designs of integrated circuits made by the intellectual property administrative department under the State Council;

(6) Cases不服 (challenging) the reexamination decisions, invalidation decisions, and renaming decisions on new plant varieties made by the New Plant Variety Reexamination Board of the agricultural and forestry administrative departments under the State Council;

(7) Cases不服 (challenging) the decisions on compulsory licensing of new plant varieties and the rulings on fees for compulsory licensing of new plant varieties made by the agricultural and forestry administrative departments under the State Council.

Article 2 Where a party dissatisfied with an effective judgment or ruling rendered by a people's court in respect of a case listed in Article 1 applies to a higher people's court for retrial, the Intellectual Property Division of the higher people's court shall be responsible for the review and trial of the retrial application.

Article 3 For the above cases tried by the Intellectual Property Divisions of the Supreme People's Court, the Beijing High People's Court, and the relevant intermediate people's courts in Beijing, the case number prefix "Zhi Xing" (知行) shall be uniformly used at the time of case filing.

Article 4 These Provisions shall come into force as of July 1, 2009. The Reply of the Supreme People's Court on the Division of Work for Patent and Trademark Related Cases after the Amendment of the Patent Law and the Trademark Law (Fa [2002] No. 117) issued on May 21, 2002 shall be repealed simultaneously.
